Query 31 — RIGHT JOIN

SELECT
    c.customer_id,
    c.first_name,
    o.order_id,
    o.order_status
FROM orders o
RIGHT JOIN customers c
    ON o.customer_id = c.customer_id;

Explanation: RIGHT JOIN keeps every row from the right-side table (customers), even if there is no matching order. An INNER JOIN would return only customers having matching orders.

Query 32 — FULL OUTER JOIN
SELECT
    c.customer_id,
    c.first_name,
    o.order_id,
    o.order_status
FROM customers c
FULL OUTER JOIN orders o
    ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id;

A FULL OUTER JOIN includes matching rows plus unmatched rows from both sides.

